viewport, checkbox and selector regressions.\n- Require the complete Python 3.8–3.14 matrix, canonical coverage JSON, existing coverage ratchets—including the 98.03% branch floor—type checks, artifact smoke tests, SDK conformance and aggregate fast checks.\n- Collection failure supplies no new coverage result. Use the new exact-head report before planning any further coverage correction.\n- Obtain the required candidate-bound full visual review: inspect the picker and comparisons, then all 46 full PNGs; require every geometry assertion and individual verdict to pass. Successful capture alone is insufficient.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward; the current reviewer explicitly left remaining source and companion review unfinished.\n- Revalidate against incoming dev changes. Bind checks, captures and reviews to the actual candidate, base, checkpoint, task and plan.\n- Preserve provenance, credentials, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator retains responsibility for completing and safely activating the RPi recommendation-policy/restart work while preserving genuine-input and security holds.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9 and every task-related companion or repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. This CI correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"5af1df680f9f476de3e392cfa42e3787eb049e270f376b23d4aa337ee5d5e613","text":"# Complete PR #9’s history correction and changelog reconciliation\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete feature checkpoint and reconcile it against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nThe saved source already contains the selected shared history lifecycle and focused regressions. The remaining confirmed source correction is the changelog conflict. Validate the existing lifecycle correction without replacing useful work.\n\nComplete check records show successful CI for published head `806f89ee273a598686fe80d7a26a382acee5a47a`; those results do not validate unpublished checkpoint changes. Independent source, companion, and full-scene review remain required. No material owner question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, remove conflict markers at lines 54, 62, and 64. Retain all seven SQL Explorer entries and dev’s replacement-authority entry under Unreleased. Preserve every historical release section and version marker. Check the complete file for additional conflict markers.\n- Preserve `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`’s shared `_record_cursor_edit` and `_prune_cursor_history` implementation. Both cursor editing and indentation must record snapshots through that lifecycle.\n- Retain snapshots only for exact edit objects present in live undo/redo stacks. Preserve active and secondary selections, selection direction, and independent preferred columns for those edits.\n- Preserve pruning after undo/redo, idle maintenance for inherited edits, and no-op transactions. No-op edits must neither create duplicate snapshots nor destroy live redo metadata. Document resets must immediately release obsolete snapshots, including during widget construction.\n- Preserve `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py` and the existing concise task changelog fragment. Make additional lifecycle changes only if source review or GitHub regression results identify a concrete defect.\n- Keep public APIs, runtime dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, protected workflows, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without adding cursors; preserve preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent multicursor movement/editing, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Paste distributes matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeats the whole text. Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal handling, metadata invalidation, and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL and thin primary/secondary carets: vertical bars where supported, underline fallback in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled capture pipeline, recovered source/documentation, diagnostic evidence, and authenticated task history. The inspected picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering. All execution occurs on GitHub.\n\n- Run cursor-history regressions first: repeated indent/undo/replacement, abandoned redo branches replaced by indentation, unindentation or editing, checkpoint eviction, document reset, explicit history clearing, inherited edits, and no-op preservation.\n- Assert observable text and cursor restoration alongside bounded metadata retention. Retain reversed selections and independent preferred-column checks.\n- Run focused multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle suites.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, canonical coverage JSON, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, and aggregate checks. Preserve branch **98.03%**, combined **98.92%**, statement **99.22%**, and all subsystem floors.\n- Use the trusted isolated candidate route for all 46 scenes. Bind capture evidence to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies, and base. Independently inspect every full PNG and geometry result before correction publication; retain comparison evidence and explicit incomplete results.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review, then complete independent implementation review covering every diff continuation, diagnostic helper/test, capture/scene change, and companion implementation. Earlier partial review supplies no approval.\n- Revalidate whenever the head or dev base changes. Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must complete and safely activate the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices. Record questions with resolver decisions; recommendations do not substitute for protected approval.\n- Monitor PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. Completing this bounded correction does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ee81771267af8eec15d44668ff4aa88017da5dbfadea162fa68e370175ffd805","text":"# Correct PR #9 document resets and CI fixtures\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `b346d04a90b5edc073a4c384eae98e3150b883f0`, against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback identifies stale secondary cursors after document replacement and two test-fixture failures. The independent resolver selected **Reset state**. No material question remains; this selection supplies no implementation, visual, merge, or protected-policy approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`, extend `load_text()` to clear secondary selections, old preferred-column mappings, and cursor-history snapshots **before** calling Textual’s implementation. Preserve Textual’s primary-cursor reset behavior and the existing method signature. Use only state initialized before `super().__init__()`; avoid mount-dependent selection helpers during construction.\n- Preserve shared history recording/pruning for edits and indentation, exact live-edit identity tracking, undo/redo restoration, inherited-edit maintenance, and no-op redo preservation. Keep idle pruning active.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, construct the eviction-test history with all required arguments: `max_checkpoints=2`, `checkpoint_timer=60.0`, and `checkpoint_max_characters=1000`. Retain explicit transaction checkpoints and every eviction, metadata-bound, text, selection, and preferred-column assertion.\n- Extend its parameterized reset regression for both `load_text()` and the `text` setter. Create mounted cursors and reversed selections across several rows with distinct preferred columns, populate undo and redo, then replace with shorter single-line text and empty text.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/completion_readiness.py`, complete the idle fixture with empty undo/redo stacks, cursor-history metadata, and a callback invoking the real pruning method. Retain assertions that idle reopens retained suggestions and leaves dismissed suggestions closed.\n- Fully read edited files through their final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n- Public APIs, runtime dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support, protected workflows, and diagnostic interfaces remain unchanged.\n\n## Required behavior retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection preserves independent preferred columns through reversal, short lines, and boundaries without creating cursors.\n- Independent multicursor movement/editing supports multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste use matching fragments, then matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Keep SQL readable with thin primary/secondary carets, vertical bars where supported and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampling, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. The inspected published-head picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Run the two failing modules first on canonical Python 3.11, Python 3.8 minimum dependencies, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest dependencies.\n- Reset regressions must assert one valid primary cursor, no secondary cursors or obsolete preferences, cleared history/snapshots, safe rendering after layout settles, and typing at only the reset cursor. Undo/redo must not resurrect the old document or cursors. Retain construction and unmounted-reset coverage.\n- Run existing history lifecycle, multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head static/lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, and aggregate checks. Obtain canonical coverage JSON; retain **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. The failed coverage test run establishes no new ratchet shortfall.\n- Capture the corrected isolated candidate on GitHub and independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and geometry results before correction publication. Bind evidence to the actual source, candidate, checkpoint, base, task, plan, and dependencies; published-head captures do not validate new edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete implementation review afterward, including every diff continuation and the RPi companion implementation. Earlier incomplete reviews supply no approval.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify completion and safe activation of recommendation-policy companion work and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices, retaining question/resolver records and security holds.\n- Monitor PR #9 and every task-related companion or repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This bounded correction does not replace that overall completion requirement.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a07d171e6d4a09c77a547e9facb213584f0e78ae82abcdb5c2ab3d0a7c6c4974","text":"# Correct PR #9’s unmounted-reset test context\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `a30ce3df206677c416b34e06b99e97e80764d1f1` against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback identifies four failures in the unmounted-reset regression. Python 3.8/3.9 lack an event loop; Python 3.10–3.12 lack an active Textual app. The independent resolver selected **Active app context**. No material question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, wrap the existing parameterized unmounted-reset test body in an asynchronous exercise invoked through `asyncio.run()`. Construct `SqlExplorerApp(FakeSession())` and enter `app.run_test()` before constructing either detached editor.\n- Keep both editors outside the mounted widget tree. Explicitly assert that each remains unmounted after construction and relevant operations.\n- Preserve all four parameter combinations, construction checks, no-op undo/redo checks, reset assertions, cursor/preferences cleanup, and empty history/snapshot assertions.\n- Retain the mounted reset/render/type regressions and shared history lifecycle unchanged. Do not catch or suppress Textual lifecycle errors, skip environments, or weaken assertions.\n- Preserve the complete checkpoint, recovered source/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Fully read edited files before writing; record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package versions.\n- Public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic interfaces, and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties; entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing. One unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste: matching fragments first, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending second, otherwise whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL with thin primary/secondary carets, supported vertical bars and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled captures, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. Inspected published-head PNGs supply no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run all four corrected cases and the complete cursor-history module on GitHub: Python 3.8 minimum/latest, canonical Python 3.11, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest. Require explicit unmounted-state assertions to pass.\n- Run adjacent lifecycle and completion-readiness tests, then focused multicursor, clipboard, movement/selection, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle coverage.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Obtain fresh canonical coverage JSON. Preserve **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. The failed test run establishes no new coverage shortfall.\n- Capture the corrected isolated candidate through the trusted GitHub route. Independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and geometry results before correction publication, retaining picker comparisons. Bind evidence to actual source, candidate, checkpoint, dev base, task, plan, and dependencies.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward. Review every diff continuation, including previously unfinished diagnostic/capture modules, associated tests, and immutable companion implementation and exact-commit CI evidence. Earlier partial review supplies no approval.\n- Revalidate whenever the head or dev base changes. Preserve complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify completion and safe activation of the RPi recommendation-policy work and restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices, preserving question/resolver records and security holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This test correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ba4a97a05feaf4f5a7f593f4efe5950150cbccf14aaf2b22dc7852d6d7a7bc9f","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer whitespace and reconcile PR #9\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `5b3b02d1a9c2afa93b6d0d4a1eac7dbfc03b828b`, preserving the complete feature checkpoint and authenticated history.\n\nThe rejected capture’s widget and compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: caret rendering replaces the separator space. The saved source already contains the selected whitespace-preserving correction and focused regressions. Preserve that work; the confirmed remaining edit is removal of three changelog conflict markers. No material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- Preserve `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`’s correction: underline every in-document character, including spaces and all visible expanded-tab cells, for primary and secondary carets. Render vertical bars only in end-of-line or empty-line padding.\n- Preserve underlying SQL, whitespace, foreground/background colors, cell widths, selections, scrolling, ruler alignment and completion behavior. Retain wrapped and horizontally clipped tab handling.\n- Preserve the existing completion scene’s `SELECT c.c FROM` text. Completion must retain its suffix and produce `SELECT c.customer_id FROM…`; the evidence does not justify changing insertion semantics or adding another separator.\n- In `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, remove conflict markers at lines 73, 77 and 88. Retain all three feature-side entries and all ten dev-side entries under Unreleased, preserving historical releases. Check the complete file for additional markers.\n- Preserve the existing concise task fragment and updated caret documentation. Fully read files before editing; retain recovered tests and documentation.\n- Keep public APIs, runtime/test dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14 and supported Textual compatibility unchanged. Preserve supersampling, diagnostics, selected narrow UI repairs, coverage targets and debt baselines.\n\n## Required feature behavior\n\n- Retain anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history retention and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Retain document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Retain shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering. Perform all validation on GitHub.\n\n- Run the existing caret-rendering and completion-spacing regressions first. Require primary/secondary spaces and tabs to retain text, colors and widths in widget and compositor output, with editor and command focus, wrapping and horizontal clipping.\n- Require completion opening to preserve the rendered separator; acceptance must preserve the suffix, cursor position and undo/redo behavior without executing a query. Retain occupied-text underline and end-of-line bar coverage.\n- Run adjacent caret-color, ruler, highlight, multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, completion-readiness, menu, checkbox/selector and capture regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint, format, type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined** and **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated capture of the corrected candidate. Independently inspect `completion-columns` and every one of the **46 full PNGs**, requiring all geometry assertions and individual visual verdicts to pass before correction publication. Retain picker comparison evidence.\n- Bind validation to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependency versions and dev base. Published-head successes do not validate saved edits.\n\n## Review, dependencies and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding. Revalidate coordinator dependencies and preserve the durable correction barrier; archived recovery receipts grant no current approval or dependent-PR release.\n- Require complete independent implementation review of every diff continuation, including diagnostic/capture modules, tests and companion implementation evidence. Earlier partial reviews remain incomplete.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve complete provenance, original questions/answers and planning records, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify the RPi recommendation-policy companion work, independent resolution records, safe activation and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve security and genuine-input holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. Completing this correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"65168e2a36952fea016fd3db3f756554f4bdd454fbf2f12bb23b38f4e2c60478","text":"# Correct primary-caret colors and reconcile PR #9 with dev\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete feature checkpoint and reconcile against pinned dev `1f7ff62aeba3c27a307a606b80459bca78b2dfd5`.\n\nPublished head `b416cd92b239290298c3e51758fb4c5db143c29a` fails three focused whitespace-caret cases across all eight matrix environments. Its hash-bound completion PNG and widget/compositor diagnostics confirm native block colors beneath the underline. Quality checks also identify formatting in the caret-rendering tests.\n\nThe independent resolver selected **Native styling**. No material implementation question remains; that selection grants no plan, implementation, visual, protected-policy, or merge approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`, replace pre-resolution cursor suppression with a private render-only theme adapter. Delegate Textual CSS resolution to a copied theme, then neutralize its cursor style before native rendering consumes it. Preserve all other resolved styles and restore the original theme in `finally`, including rendering failures. Keep the absent-theme path intact.\n- Preserve the existing underline overlay for every in-document character, space, and visible expanded-tab cell. Keep vertical bars exclusively in end-of-line and empty-line padding. Preserve text, foreground/background colors, widths, selection/search styling, scrolling, ruler mapping, and completion behavior.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`, retain every existing assertion and apply canonical Ruff formatting. Extend mounted coverage using the actual `TextArea.render_line`, checking syntax-colored text and the `SELECT c.c FROM` separator alongside existing space/tab cases.\n- Reconcile stale automation changes with pinned dev: restore `.github/agent/review_control.py`, `tests/repository/notification_metadata.py`, and `tests/repository/label_reconciliation.py` exactly to the pinned base. Their current differences remove newer notification and provenance safeguards.\n- Reconcile operations documentation using pinned dev’s current contract and source associations. Preserve useful feature-specific activation requirements without reinstating obsolete “staged, not active” claims.\n- Reconcile the changelog using pinned dev’s history plus every distinct feature entry. Remove only conflict markers and exact duplicates; retain historical releases and record this correction through the managed fragment mechanism.\n- Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered source, documentation, diagnostics, authenticated history, and useful checkpoint changes.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, diagnostic interfaces, coverage targets, and debt baselines remain unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without creating cursors. Preserve independent preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, bounded snapshot retention, and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste distribute matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeat the complete text. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, supersampling, bounded comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. Preserve completion suffixes and existing SQL separators. The inspected picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run caret-rendering, caret-color, render-lifecycle, and completion-spacing regressions on GitHub with minimum/current supported Textual dependencies.\n- Require real widget and compositor output to preserve primary/secondary caret text, colors, and widths under editor and command focus. Cover spaces, expanded tabs, wrapping, horizontal clipping, syntax text, selections, search highlights, and padding bars.\n- Verify original theme identity and state after repeated renders, focus changes, missing styles, absent themes, and native-render exceptions. Preserve existing mocked unit tests alongside real-renderer coverage.\n- Run restored notification/provenance regressions and adjacent multicursor, clipboard, movement/history/reset, ruler, completion, menu, checkbox/selector, and capture suites.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors. The failed coverage test run establishes no new coverage shortfall.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated GitHub capture of the corrected candidate. Inspect `completion-columns`, then all **46 full PNGs**, requiring every geometry assertion and individual visual verdict to pass before correction publication. Retain picker comparisons.\n- Bind validation to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, task, plan, dependency versions, and dev base. Published-head evidence does not validate saved edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward, covering every diff continuation and companion implementation evidence.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve durable dependency/correction barriers, complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion, safe activation, recorded independent resolutions, and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices. Historical receipts do not release current holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This bounded correction does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"65b765782ecd88e9b234d2c3e237161bb1fbe780dae4e4d6874b6733b527774c","text":"# Correct PR #9’s remaining formatting failure\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `f0f0abc4346f085df2e9058b9613532b04f2c227` against pinned dev `1f7ff62aeba3c27a307a606b80459bca78b2dfd5`.\n\nComplete feedback and failed-job logs identify one blocker: Ruff formatting in `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`. Matrix, SDK, type, coverage, and artifact validation passed. The latest exact-head review reports complete source, companion, and 46-scene review without concrete blockers.\n\nNo material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- Apply canonical Ruff 0.15.22 formatting only to `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`, using the existing Python 3.8 target, 100-character line length, and LF configuration. Private coding workers make source-only edits; formatting verification runs on GitHub.\n- Preserve every test, parameter combination, fixture value, assertion, and negative control. In particular, retain real native-renderer and compositor checks for syntax colors, whitespace, primary/secondary carets, and original theme restoration.\n- Preserve the complete feature checkpoint and authenticated history. Do not reopen resolved production caret, completion, picker, menu, or controller corrections without new evidence.\n- Record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism, preserving historical entries and package/README versions.\n- Keep public APIs, method signatures, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, diagnostic schemas, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged.\n- Fully read edited files before writing and revalidate against any changed head or dev base.\n\n## Required feature behavior retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history retention, reset cleanup, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin underlines over every in-document character and expanded-tab cell, with original colors and widths. Reserve vertical bars for line-end/empty-line padding.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled capture, recovered documentation/tests, and bounded diagnostic evidence.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First verify canonical formatting and lint for the affected module. Require zero new findings without changing baselines.\n- Run its existing regressions alongside caret-color, render-lifecycle, and completion-spacing coverage on minimum/current supported dependencies. No additional tests are needed for formatting alone.\n- Require fresh exact-head quality, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, artifact, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branches**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statements**, plus subsystem floors. Current passing coverage supplies no reason for additional coverage corrections.\n- Obtain the required candidate-bound GitHub visual capture and independent review of all **46 full PNGs** and geometry results. Retain picker comparisons; prior-head evidence cannot certify the corrected head.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and implementation review afterward, confirming the correction preserves assertions and the complete feature.\n- Bind checks, captures, and reviews to the actual source, checkpoint, candidate, dev base, task, plan, and dependencies.\n- Preserve provenance, durable correction/dependency barriers, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion and safe activation, recorded independent resolutions, and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9 and all task-related companion/correction PRs through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This formatting correction does not complete the broader monitoring objective.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","questions":[{"answer_index":16,"id":"fbd480038ee660edb95dd3690683161a39480ffc41dfac01f8e147887794ef84","text":"Can the coordinator expose a fresh database-picker capture with its heading widget rows, compositor rows, exported SVG, and hash-bound final PNG through source_files evidence? The available layer evidence is historical, and its PNG is inaccessible. The reviewed plan requires identifying the first failing layer before changing picker presentation or capture/export."},{"answer_index":18,"id":"9a11147e3ffd85ce140c8f1244a1b15377efd00916e606a8b431a2d03a92488d","text":"The fresh receipt binds capture `38731476440` to candidate `3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5` and the saved checkpoint. Widget rows, compositor rows and parsed SVG all retain the complete heading, including the `c`. This does not establish a production picker defect.\n\n1. **Coordinator tooling question:** Can `read_evidence_image` be exposed in this planner session for the supplied hash-bound PNG? It is absent from the available tools, and `read_image` returns “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” PNG inspection is still needed before specifying a presentation or export correction.\n\nNo owner decision or replacement upload is needed. Raw SVG bytes are not supplied. The publication transport repair also remains coordinator-owned; complete task history must be preserved."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"16d4d781180edfb004dda9a37d5c640ea072ea2cc5775a4681e92c27f584ab07","text":"Can the coordinator provide the reviewed plan’s GitHub reproduction with actual raw and framed SVG bytes, renderer versions, and available/selected font diagnostics, bound to the candidate, checkpoint and PNG hashes? PNG inspection now works and confirms the obscured `c`; terminal rows and parsed SVG preserve it. The supplied artifacts still cannot distinguish framing from rasterization, so a correction would be speculative."},{"answer_index":20,"id":"9d7dfd33ccfb0fff403dc64cf5154bb0084c6d340b3db71751df45304dbb3650","text":"Coordinator: please expose the exact pre-invocation checkpoint source for tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py. I mistakenly treated a capped 300-line read as complete and omitted its remaining lines when writing. Restore that file’s original suffix before retaining my focused additions. Please also verify the restored README against the saved checkpoint. No owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":21,"id":"962ad2658075e133178b0c27a43c436c00ea5a63640a4a6e0dafbca91a41dc09","text":"Coordinator: please run the approved isolated GitHub candidate capture from the preserved checkpoint, including the restored diagnostic tests and existing SVG-evidence helper/tests. Expose hash-bound database-picker raw/framed SVG content, font/renderer diagnostics and PNG through source_files. The reviewed plan requires this evidence before selecting a heading correction; no owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":22,"id":"d82141d33b770fcc68e14949f0292959e0f2597aa4301b71d32ab7338f57b0e7","text":"1. The current logs prove checkbox text loss but do not identify its first failing layer; they also report coverage totals without exact missing arcs. Which correction sequence should the plan use?\nEvidence first (Recommended): Fix behavior-preserving Ruff/format issues, add bounded failing-state diagnostics and focused task-related regressions, and obtain exact-head GitHub reproduction plus coverage JSON before selecting a checkbox production repair.\nSeparate diagnostic checkpoint: Keep this step diagnostic-only; obtain checkbox state and coverage evidence on GitHub, then independently plan all lint, test and production corrections together."},{"answer_index":23,"id":"e896f2e46da935a3d8d2023d77a872fd7f6624fbdae4625988d391767b3be2a6","text":"I read the complete current-head check records and all failed-job log parts. Existing feature requirements remain settled; no new owner preference is needed. Three coordinator evidence questions remain before a concrete repair plan:\n\n1. **Picker correction:** Can the coordinator expose capture `38927473247`’s hash-bound receipt, database-picker geometry, complete raw/framed SVGs, and all four comparison PNGs? The visual evidence tools currently return “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” The reviewer’s framing finding needs direct inspection before selecting the export correction.\n\n2. **Coverage:** Can the coordinator expose canonical `coverage.json` from run `38927048857`, bound to head `e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2`? Branch coverage is **98.02% against 98.03%**. Exact missing arcs are needed to specify meaningful task-related regressions without changing baselines.\n\n3. **Type-menu failure:** Can the coordinator provide a bounded GitHub reproduction capturing focus, `type_input`, matches, scroll offsets, field/viewport geometry, and queued layout state immediately before the failing initial `assert menu.display` on Python 3.13/3.14? This will distinguish fixture timing from a production positioning defect before choosing a repair.\n\nThese are coordinator artifact requests, not requests for owner uploads or approval. No files were changed and no programs were executed."},{"answer_index":24,"id":"b239df38a3cbbd33de3627b25a36e9063e036dac68b6e9c97c83d69c701c88f3","text":"1. The rejected PNG and widget/compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: rendering replaces the existing separator space with a bar. Should the correction preserve every in-document whitespace cell using the thin underline fallback, reserving vertical bars for end-of-line and empty-line padding?\nPreserve whitespace (Recommended): Keep spaces and expanded tabs intact for primary and secondary carets; retain colors, cell widths and completion behavior, and add focused rendering and completion regressions."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"sql explorer: 1) if ctrl+shift+arrow up/down is pressed, then we should not spawn multiple cursors, instead selection should be expanded to the left until the line start, and next line until cursor's column (vs code like), it can be repeated multiple times to select many lines 2) now it seems that when multiple cursors is spawned, then I ctrl+c something and ctrl+v each cursor inserts WHOLE clipboard. instead each should have its own clipboard (VS code like)","task_id":"e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","version":2}